  "facts": [
    "Berkley Bridge, a double‑leaf bascule marvel, first opened in 1952 as part of the Norfolk–Portsmouth Bridge‑Tunnel project, and remains toll‑free after its bonds were fully repaid.",
    "In 1991, I‑264 expansion added a parallel span, turning Berkley Bridge into an eight‑lane conduit and introducing a new interchange with I‑464 to link Chesapeake with the Berkley area.",
    "A 2014 bicycle collision involving a bridge tender’s vehicle prompted VDOT to ban tenders from driving on the pedestrian walkway and mandate spotters for any future bridge‑vehicle movements."
